## Notes

---

## Acceptance Criteria (Overall Spec)

### Must Pass Before Release:
✅ No duplicate content across multiple pipeline runs  
✅ No old articles (before ABSOLUTE_CUTOFF_DATE) ever appear  
✅ QA Agent requests backups when validation fails  
✅ CEO Agent ALEX responds to board queries via CLI  
✅ All API failures handled gracefully (no pipeline crashes)  
✅ State management tracks sent content reliably  
✅ Integration tests pass (full pipeline + failure recovery)  
✅ Documentation complete and accurate  

### Performance Targets:
- Pipeline completes in < 5 minutes (daily digest)
- Agent response time < 30 seconds each
- API success rate > 95% (with fallbacks)
- Zero downtime (graceful degradation)

---

## Rollout Plan

### Week 1: Phase 1 (Critical Fixes)
- Days 1-2: Tasks 1.1, 1.2, 1.3 (API validation, DB migration, state manager)
- Days 3-4: Tasks 1.4, 1.5 (cleanup filter, QA backup mechanism)
- Day 5: Integration testing, bug fixes

**Milestone:** System works reliably, no duplicates, QA backups functional

---

### Week 2: Phase 2 (Multi-Agent Architecture)
- Days 1-2: Tasks 2.1, 2.2, 2.3 (message router, CEO Agent, CLI)
- Days 3-4: Tasks 2.4, 2.5 (reporter agents, fact-checker)
- Day 5: Task 2.6 (refactor coordinator), integration

**Milestone:** Full autonomous multi-agent system operational

---

### Week 3: Phase 3 & 4 (Polish & Testing)
- Days 1-2: Tasks 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4 (observability, degraded mode, errors)
- Days 3-4: Tasks 4.1, 4.2 (unit + integration tests)
- Day 5: Task 4.3 (documentation), final testing

**Milestone:** Production-ready system with comprehensive tests

---

### Future: Phase 5 (Enhancements)
- Implement as needed based on user feedback
- Scout Agent, LangGraph, Weekly mode, Web dashboard

---

## Risk Mitigation

### Risk: API rate limits during development
**Mitigation:** Use test mode (save to file), mock LLM calls in tests, implement caching

### Risk: Database migration breaks existing data
**Mitigation:** Backup database before migration, test on copy first, make migration idempotent

### Risk: Agent communication overhead slows pipeline
**Mitigation:** Profile performance, optimize message passing, use async where possible

### Risk: Degraded mode produces low-quality content
**Mitigation:** Add quality checks even in degraded mode, notify board member, require approval

---

## Success Metrics (Post-Launch)

### Week 1 After Launch:
- 0 duplicate stories reported
- 0 old articles reported
- 100% pipeline success rate (including fallbacks)
- <5 CEO Agent queries from board member (autonomous)

### Month 1 After Launch:
- 95%+ API success rate
- <2 minute average pipeline execution
- 90%+ story quality score (board member feedback)
- Scout Agent discovers 5+ new sources (if implemented)

